    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0212",
      "sequence": 224,
      "meaning": "Rāma and Lakṣmaṇa went with the sage to the world-purifying Gaṅgā. Gādhi’s son told the entire story of how the celestial river came to earth. The Lord bathed there with the seers and the Brahmins received gifts of many kinds. Joyfully they continued with a company of sages and soon drew near Videha’s city. Seeing its beauty, Rāma and his younger brother were especially delighted. Many stepwells, wells, rivers and ponds held nectar-like water and jewel steps. Lovely intoxicated bees hummed over nectar, birds of many colors sang sweetly, groves of every kind bloomed in varied hues, and the threefold breeze always brought delight. Flower gardens, orchards and ample woods, rich in birds, blossomed, fruited and put forth fresh leaves all around the city.",
