    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0213",
      "sequence": 225,
      "meaning": "The city’s excellence cannot be described: wherever the mind turns, it is enticed. Lovely markets and wondrous balconies seem fashioned by Providence with his own hands from jewels. Wealthy, excellent merchants, like Kubera, sit with goods of every kind. Its handsome squares and pleasing lanes are continually sprinkled with fragrance. Every home is auspicious, painted as though Love himself were the artist. The city’s men and women are handsome, pure and saintly—righteous, wise and virtuous. Janaka’s residence is so incomparable that even gods grow dazed upon seeing its delights; the mind is astonished by the fortress, as though it had gathered the beauty of all worlds. Sītā’s beautiful dwelling, made in many arrangements of white buildings, jewels, gold and cloth, is beyond description.",
