    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0214",
      "sequence": 226,
      "meaning": "Every splendid gateway has diamond-hard doors, and crowds of kings, actors, bards and panegyrists fill the approaches. Huge stables for horses and elephants have always been built, crowded with steeds, elephants and chariots. Many warriors, ministers and commanders possess homes resembling the royal palace. Outside the city, beside ponds and rivers, numerous kings have camped here and there. Seeing an incomparable mango grove, comfortable and lovely in every way, Kauśika said it pleased him and proposed that they stay there. ‘Very well, lord,’ said the abode of grace, and he alighted with the company of sages. The Mithilā king learned that the great sage Viśvāmitra had come and set out joyfully to meet the sage-leader, accompanied by ministers, pure priests, many warriors, eminent Brahmins, his guru and kinsmen.",
