    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0215",
      "sequence": 227,
      "meaning": "Janaka bowed, placing his head at Viśvāmitra’s feet, and the delighted sage blessed him. The king reverently greeted every Brahmin and rejoiced in his great fortune. After repeatedly asking after their welfare, Viśvāmitra seated him. At that moment the two brothers returned from seeing the flower garden: dark and fair, tender adolescents who delighted the eyes and stole the world’s heart. Everyone rose when Raghupati arrived, and Viśvāmitra seated the brothers near himself. All were happy at the sight, eyes wet and bodies thrilled. Seeing those sweet, enchanting forms, the disembodied Videha became more than ever detached from bodily awareness. Knowing the king’s mind submerged in love, Janaka recovered discernment and courage, bowed to the sage, and spoke in a deep voice broken by emotion.",
